 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, choose the correct interval notation for the graph.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508116,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<img src=\"exercises/media/f48b1e017fabf359.jpg\" alt=\"A number line ranges from negative 1 to 2, in increments of 1. A close parenthesis is marked at 1. The region to the left of the parenthesis is shaded on the number line.\">\n<br>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n<li><span data-math=\"[ - 1,\\infty )\">[ - 1,\\infty )</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ ( - 1,1)}\">{ ( - 1,1)}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ (\\infty ,1)}\">{ (\\infty ,1)}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ ( - \\infty ,1)}\">{ ( - \\infty ,1)}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ ( - \\infty , - 1)}\">{ ( - \\infty , - 1)}</span></li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The parenthesis indicates that 1 is not included in the solution. The region shaded is to the left of 1, so that means the solution includes numbers less than 1. In interval notation, this looks like <span data-math=\"\\left( { - \\infty , - 1} \\right)\">\\left( { - \\infty , 1} \\right)</span>.</p>\n<p>Notice that the interval notation version is in the same order as the graph. Negative infinity is on the left and 1 is on the right.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "d <span data-math=\"\\left( { - \\infty , - 1} \\right)\">\\left( { - \\infty , - 1} \\right)</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 508117,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<img src=\"exercises/media/edae236948b0c6ce.jpg\" alt=\"A number line ranges from negative 6 to negative 3, in increments of 1. An open square bracket is marked at negative 5. The region to the right of the square bracket is shaded on the number line.\">\n<br>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n<li><span data-math=\"( - 5,\\infty )\">( - 5,\\infty )</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ [ - 5,\\infty )}\">{ [ - 5,\\infty )}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ [ - 5,\\infty )}\">{ [ - 5,\\infty )}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ [ - 5, - 3)}\">{ [ - 5, - 3)}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ [ - 5, - 3]}\">{ [ - 5, - 3]}</span></li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The bracket indicates that 5 is included in the solution. The region shaded is to right of 5, so that means the solution includes numbers greater than 5. In interval notation, this looks like <span data-math=\"[5,\\infty )\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Notice that the interval notation version is in the same order as the graph. The number 5 is on the left and positive infinity is on the right.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "b <span data-math=\"[ - 5,\\infty )\">[ - 5,\\infty )</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 508118,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<img src=\"exercises/media/b0d03c9143e5405f.jpg\" alt=\"A number line ranges from 0 to 3, in increments of 1. An open square bracket is marked at 1.5. The region to the right of the square bracket is shaded on the number line.\">\n<br>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n<li><span data-math=\"(1,\\infty )\">(1,\\infty )</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ [1,\\infty )}\">{ [1,\\infty )}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ \\left[ {\\frac{3}{2},\\infty } \\right)}\">{ \\left[ {\\frac{3}{2},\\infty } \\right)}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ \\left( {\\frac{3}{2},\\infty } \\right)}\">{ \\left( {\\frac{3}{2},\\infty } \\right)}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ \\left( {\\infty ,\\frac{3}{2}} \\right)}\">{ \\left( {\\infty ,\\frac{3}{2}} \\right)}</span></li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The bracket indicates that <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span> is included in the solution. The region shaded is to right of <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span>, so that means the solution includes numbers greater than <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span>. In interval notation, this looks like <span data-math=\"\\left[ {\\frac{3}{2},\\infty } \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Notice that the interval notation version is in the same order as the graph. The number <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span> is on the left and positive infinity is on the right.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "c <span data-math=\"\\left[ {\\frac{3}{2},\\infty } \\right)\">\\left[ {\\frac{3}{2},\\infty } \\right)</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 508119,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<img src=\"exercises/media/1e713545b647dfa3.jpg\" alt=\"A number line ranges from negative 5 to 4, in increments of 1. An open parenthesis is marked at negative 4 and a close parenthesis is marked at 3. The region within the parentheses is shaded on the number line.\">\n<br>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n<li><span data-math=\"{( - 4,3)}\">{( - 4,3)}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ (3, - 4)}\">{ (3, - 4)}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{[ - \\infty ,\\infty )}\">{[ - \\infty ,\\infty )}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ [ - 4,3]}\">{ [ - 4,3]}</span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"{ [3, - 4]}\">{ [3, - 4]}</span></li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The solution is shaded between parentheses at –4 and 3. This corresponds in interval notation to those numbers between parentheses with a comma in between.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( { - 4,3} \\right)\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "a <span data-math=\"( - 4,3)\">( - 4,3)</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
